;; Clojure's AOT level's divergences (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1, RPS3, RPS4, RPS16): the
;; classes of the level's non-passes, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (test/clojure/
;; divergences.edn says how a case is written and matched). The level's check is Clojure's suite
;; compiled (REAP3, test/arbace-go-aot-results.edn, not yet built); beside it diffcheck's Clojure
;; pair (bin/diffcheck, test/diffcheck/known.edn: the evaluated half against the compiled one),
;; its known disagreements as cases "known REASON". Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :interned-at-load
  :title "compiled code interns the vars it names when its namespace's loader starts"
  :kind :design
  :why "as the JVM's AOT: a compiled loader makes its constants, the vars they name among them, when it starts (Compiler$AOT/pool), so fresh.ns/fv, scratch.space/in-scratch and user/map exist before the cases that define them; evaluated code interns a var when the form naming it is analyzed. Recorded as known (doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, \"One-segment namespaces\", \"F3 and F4 measured together\"); no decision names it by design (RPS20)"
  :decided :pending
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, compilation's semantics, as the JVM's AOT"]}
 {:id :compiled-loader-line
  :title "Compiler/LINE in a compiled loader"
  :kind :design
  :why "eval at run time of a form without positions reports Compiler/LINE and COLUMN, which Compiler.load sets for each top-level form but a compiled loader does not (as the JVM's __init class). Recorded as known (doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, F2's findings, \"the check's own\"); no decision names it by design (RPS20)"
  :decided :pending
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, a position in a message"]}
 {:id :shared-symbols
  :title "symbols shared in a compiled class's constant pool"
  :kind :design
  :why "a class's symbols without metadata are made once (SA155), so two equal quoted symbols of compiled code are identical; Clojure leaves symbols' identity unspecified"
  :decided "doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, F3.3 (a) (the user, 2026-10-17)"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, the compiled constants \(SA155\)"]}
 {:id :q1-compiled-prims
  :title "compiled fns are primitive where the evaluator's are not (Q1)"
  :kind :design
  :why "a ^long fn compiled implements IFn$LL and IFn$LOL as on the JVM; evaluated it is a fn made at run time, which does not (the eval level's Q1)"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-PLAN.md, Q1 (a) (the user, 2026-10-09)"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, native\.ae's copy \(c2j:\), by design of the evaluator"]}
 {:id :identity-hash
  :title "identity hashes (not reproducible)"
  :kind :design
  :why "a StringBuilder's identity hash differs in each run"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-NOTES.md, phase 2B (as decided for #object printing)"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, not reproducible: an identity hash"]}
 {:id :f2.4-limit
  :title "j2g's limit left by F2.4: compiled classes naming the namespace's vars or holding deftype*"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a compiled deftype or fn whose Clojure code names the namespace's vars, or holds a deftype* in a fn, is left out of j2g's analysis, and the code naming it fails where it runs"
  :decided "RPS6 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md: to be fixed in REAP3"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, native\.ae's copy \(c2j:\), a limit of j2g left by F2\.4"]}
]
